      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done",
      "parentUuid": "d64d7fe1_4aca6042",
      "revId": "8972941f48ef63f5ce12cc09ca1124e200b670ce",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e5da62eb_53f2e6d1",
        "filename": "api/src/main/yang/service_path/transportpce-tapi-sbi@2026-04-10.yang",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 65,
      "author": {
        "id": 9118
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-01T08:10:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Wouldn\u0027t it be better to add a list of sbi controller details here?\nFor now, we can define it as a list with max elements as 1.\nAnd define url, userid, password, tapi-version, controller-type etc.\n\nOr, do you prefer keeping it outside of this?",
      "revId": "8972941f48ef63f5ce12cc09ca1124e200b670ce",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d384c9e2_bfd606f5",
        "filename": "api/src/main/yang/service_path/transportpce-tapi-sbi@2026-04-10.yang",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 65,
      "author": {
        "id": 7217
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-16T09:14:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The introduction of a list of SBI controller is planned, and I fully agree with you on the fact that this will be needed at a time. However, this has strong impact on the code, as we will need to revise a lot of things : number of Tapi-SBI-topologies, the way we process their names, how we handle path-computation considering that we may have as many sbi-topologies (and their corresponding TAPI-SBI-ABS-NODE in OpenROADM topology) as we have southbound controllers.\n\nSo, in a first step, I think we should keep it as simple as possible, focusing on addressing next IOWN demos.\n\nAt the time we will consider the extension of the number of connected SBI controllers, we may need to refine controller customization module (Directly pushing yang models in OR, or using augmentations in the meanwhile). We will need also to add other elements in yang models. this might be here, or in another dedicated module.\n\nIn any case, IMHO, this should be in separate future change as the impact is huge.",
      "parentUuid": "e5da62eb_53f2e6d1",
      "revId": "8972941f48ef63f5ce12cc09ca1124e200b670ce",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1f6be39e_353b91ec",
        "filename": "api/src/main/yang/service_path/transportpce-tapi-sbi@2026-04-10.yang",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 116,
      "author": {
        "id": 9118
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-15T09:51:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Are you assuming that SIPs are bi-directional and NEPs could be uni-directional?\nWhy not allow separate SIPs for each direction?",
      "revId": "8972941f48ef63f5ce12cc09ca1124e200b670ce",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4e83cfcc_892c1d1e",
        "filename": "api/src/main/yang/service_path/transportpce-tapi-sbi@2026-04-10.yang",
