      "writtenOn": "2026-07-16T09:14:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I used the assumption that we define only bidirectional services, and that there is no interest in having unidirectional SIP. However, you are right, we should be as generic as possible, and T-API allows to do so. As we also depends on some parameters that may be defined by the SBI controller, we need to consider this case. Corrected it to put it at rx/tx level according to your suggestion.",
      "parentUuid": "1f6be39e_353b91ec",
      "revId": "8972941f48ef63f5ce12cc09ca1124e200b670ce",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
